+### [Multi-scale Neural Field Reconstruction](7437-multi-scale-neural-field-reconstruction.md)
+Multi-scale Neural Field Reconstruction is a framework that constructs pyramid-structured encoding volumes to provide geometric information at all scales for Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF), addressing the limitation of single-scale volumes in scenes with diverse object sizes. It learns an encoding volume and reconstructs density and radiance fields separately, using multi-scale geometric information acquired during training (rendering at each level) and used only at the final level during testing. It sets itself apart from siblings like [Explicit Radiance Fields](806-explicit-radiance-fields.md) by explicitly modeling scale via a pyramid of 3D volumes rather than a single grid or octree, and from [Plenoxels](7440-plenoxels.md) by retaining differentiable neural field reconstruction at each scale rather than relying on spherical harmonics or explicit voxel colors directly. See [Multi-scale Neural Field Reconstruction](7437-multi-scale-neural-field-reconstruction.md).
 
 ### [Plenoxels](7440-plenoxels.md)
-Plenoxels is an explicit radiance field representation that replaces the neural network used in NeRF with a sparse 3D voxel grid storing density and spherical harmonic (SH) coefficients. It solves the computational bottleneck of neural network inference during training and rendering, achieving training speeds two orders of magnitude faster than NeRF while maintaining comparable image quality. Unlike implicit representations, Plenoxels allows for direct data access via trilinear interpolation, trading increased memory consumption for significant gains in optimization and rendering efficiency.
+Plenoxels is an explicit radiance field representation that replaces the neural network used in NeRF with a sparse 3D voxel grid storing density and spherical harmonic (SH) coefficients. It solves the computational bottleneck of neural network inference during rendering and optimization, enabling training speeds two orders of magnitude faster than NeRF and real-time rendering capabilities. Unlike implicit representations, Plenoxels relies on direct data access and trilinear interpolation, trading increased memory consumption for significant gains in efficiency. See [Plenoxels](7440-plenoxels.md).
